[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every date report into one ticket. Grouped by the tenant's
locale and booking form, the same reports are two different bugs. The table below is built
from the export when the page renders.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The two problems

<strong>parser</strong>: the shared parser reads every date month first, so a day-first tenant's dates
come out flipped. This is what #4471 describes, and it covers most of the reports. Five of them read as a
one-day move and are counted here too.

<strong>hint</strong>: tenants on the booking-v3 form see the hint MM/DD/YYYY under the date field, so
their people type month first and the form reads it day first. This is a different bug with a
different fix, and it has no ticket of its own on the desk.

<Callout kind="warn">
Intake's browser guess is not the cause. Some reports tagged as parser are hint reports, and the other way round.
Count by tenant, not by tag.
</Callout>

## What to do

- Keep #4471 for `parser`.
- Open a separate ticket for `hint`.

